  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $18.6B in contracts in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 12.8% year over year. Award activity included 26,395 contracts, with an average award size of $704K. Recent fiscal-year history shows obligations of $34.3B in FY21, $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, and $21.3B in FY25. Contract spending in FY2026 to date concentrates in technology and health science services. Computer Systems Design Services received $2.8B, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services received $1.6B, and Other Computer Related Services received $1.5B. Research categories and health-specific industries also rank highly, including Research and Development in Biotechnology at $1.3B, Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $1.2B, and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $612M. Large vendors carry significant shares of the FY2026 to date total. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $892M, MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE received $492M, and NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC received $329M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has HHS contract spending changed recently?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $18.6B in FY2026 to date, down 12.8% year over year. Obligations peaked at $34.3B in FY21 and have trended lower through FY25 and FY26. Award count in FY2026 to date stands at 26,395 with an average award size of $704K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the dominant contract categories and top vendors?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services leads with $2.8B, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $1.6B and Other Computer Related Services at $1.5B. Research and health-related categories together account for several top slots, including Research and Development in Biotechnology at $1.3B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $612M. GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is the largest vendor at $892M, with MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC at $329M."
      }
    ]
